cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use GeoVersa (DB-TARF) or ConvKrigingNet2D in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "GeoVersa: Design-Based Residual-Correction Forests for Digital Soil Mapping"
version: 0.3.0
date-released: 2026-07-06
url: https://github.com/HugoMachadoRodrigues/GeoVersa
repository-code: https://github.com/HugoMachadoRodrigues/GeoVersa
license: MIT
type: software
abstract: >-
  GeoVersa ships DB-TARF (Design-Based Targeted Adaptive Residual Forest), a
  random forest augmented by a cross-fitted, out-of-fold-selected residual
  correction (residual forests, Cubist, ordinary kriging, MLP, and a
  variogram-informed radial-basis smoother) together with design-based
  conformal prediction intervals. It is evaluated under the design-based
  paradigm of Wadoux et al. (2021) on their public Amazonian above-ground
  woody biomass benchmark. The repository also preserves the ConvKrigingNet2D
  research line — a hybrid deep architecture fusing a 2D CNN raster-patch
  encoder, a tabular MLP, and a coordinate MLP through a differentiable
  anisotropic residual kriging layer.
keywords:
  - Digital Soil Mapping
  - Pedometrics
  - Kriging
  - Deep Learning
  - Geostatistics
  - Spatial Statistics
  - Convolutional Neural Network
  - R
  - torch
